# --- environment ---
.venv/
# LangFlow lives in its own environment on purpose: it resolves several hundred
# packages and pins against versions the measurement path is fixed to. Nothing this
# repository publishes depends on it. scripts/run_langflow_check.py names the two
# commands that create this directory when it is absent.
.venv-langflow/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
node_modules/
.next/
dist/
build/

# --- data plane: never commit the snapshot or the artifacts it derives ---
# Root-anchored. An unanchored `data/` also matched apps/web/public/data, which
# is the console's committed build input, so the deploy silently had no numbers.
/data/
!/data/.gitkeep
*.parquet
*.npy
*.npz
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.png
!docs/**/*.png
!tests/fixtures/**/*.png
!apps/web/public/**/*.png

# --- generated artifacts: manifests are committed, payloads are not ---
artifacts/**/*
# Directories must be re-included first. Git does not descend into an
# excluded directory, so without this every negation below is dead and
# the evidence silently never stages.
!artifacts/**/
!artifacts/.gitkeep
!artifacts/**/*.json
!artifacts/**/*.md
!artifacts/a3_overlays/*.png

# Reviewer annotations are private local notes and are never committed. They are
# already excluded by the catch-all above, but only incidentally, and a future
# re-include written for some other .jsonl would start committing them silently.
# This says so on purpose, and it wins because it comes last.
artifacts/annotations/
*.jsonl

# --- secrets ---
.env
.env.local
*.key
*.pem
credentials*.json

# --- os / editor ---
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# working brief, not part of the judged submission
BOB_START_HERE.md

# --- A3 investigation cache: API pages and waterfall PNGs, not evidence ---
.a3_cache/

# --- console build output ---
# apps/web/out is what `next build` writes: it is the deploy artifact, derived
# entirely from public/ and the receipts, and committing it would put a second
# copy of every waterfall in the history. The imagery under public/ is committed
# because the console cannot be rebuilt without it; the export is not.
apps/web/out/
apps/web/tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.playwright-mcp/

# Manim render scratch. The scene source is committed and the finished video is
# committed to apps/web/public/media, which is what the site serves. The render tree
# holds partial movie files, per-text SVG caches and converted font binaries, all of
# which are reproducible from scripts/explainer_corridor.py and none of which a
# reviewer needs.
/media/

# A received critique, kept out of the tree on purpose. It is the input to a unit rather
# than a claim this project makes, and every statement worth keeping from it has been
# answered in docs/BOB_BUILD_LOG.md or in a claim register row. Ignored rather than
# deleted, because the file is still the record of what was asked for.
HANDOVER_*.md

# --- internal, deliberately untracked ---
# Four documents were removed from the tracked tree on 2026-08-22. None of them is
# evidence about the product and each one costs a judge something to read:
#
#   docs/BUILD_BUDGET.md         how build credits were budgeted across trial accounts.
#                                Permitted by the July 28 FAQ and still the wrong thing to
#                                publish in a repository submitted to IBM: it invites a
#                                question no judge needs to ask and answers none they have.
#   docs/SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md how judges were expected to score, what a competitor named
#                                its repository, and when to flip this one public.
#                                Publishing the strategy for winning inside the entry.
#   docs/WAVE_C1_PROMPT.md       build prompts for two units, carrying test counts (563 and
#   docs/WAVE_D_PROMPT.md        922) that the tree has since passed. Two tracked files
#                                disagreeing about one measured quantity is the exact
#                                defect the claim register exists to prevent.
#
# docs/BOB_TASK_PROMPTS.md stays: it is the prompt library, and how Bob was used is a
# scored requirement. Copies of all four live outside the repository.
docs/BUILD_BUDGET.md
docs/SUBMISSION_CHECKLIST.md
docs/WAVE_C1_PROMPT.md
docs/WAVE_D_PROMPT.md
